1. NORTHBRIDGE CAPITAL PARTNERS LIMITED AND SUBSIDIARIES, A CORPORATION ORGANIZED UNDER THE LAWS OF IRELAND ("BORROWERS"), AND THE LENDER, A FINANCIAL INSTITUTION ORGANIZED UNDER THE LAWS OF NEW YORK ("LENDER"), ENTER INTO THIS LOAN AGREEMENT ON THE DATE HEREINAFTER STATED ("EFFECTIVE DATE").

2. WHEREAS, BORROWERS ARE ENGAGED IN THE BUSINESS OF INVESTMENT MANAGEMENT AND HAVE REQUESTED FROM LENDER A LOAN TO FUND OPERATIONS AND EXPANSION, AND LENDER IS WILLING TO EXTEND SUCH LOAN UPON THE TERMS AND CONDITIONS HEREINAFTER SET FORTH.

3. NOW, THEREFORE, IN CONSIDERATION OF THE MUTUAL COVENANTS AND AGREEMENTS CONTAINED HEREIN, THE PARTIES HERETO AGREE AS FOLLOWS:

4. 1. LOAN TERMS
4.1. PRINCIPAL AMOUNT: BORROWERS SHALL OBTAIN A LOAN OF SEVENTY-FIVE MILLION DOLLARS ($75,000,000) (THE "PRINCIPAL AMOUNT") FROM LENDER.

4.2. REPAYMENT: BORROWERS SHALL REPAY THE PRINCIPAL AMOUNT IN FULL WITHIN THREE YEARS FROM THE EFFECTIVE DATE, COMMENCING ON THE DATE THAT IS ONE YEAR AFTER THE EFFECTIVE DATE, AND PAYABLE IN EQUAL MONTHLY INSTALLMENTS, EACH IN THE AMOUNT OF TWO MILLION FIVE HUNDRED THOUSAND DOLLARS ($2,500,000).

4.3. INTEREST RATE: THE PRINCIPAL AMOUNT SHALL ACCRUE INTEREST AT AN ANNUAL RATE OF FIVE PERCENT (5%) FROM THE EFFECTIVE DATE UNTIL THE DATE OF REPAYMENT.

5. 2. INTEREST AND FEES
5.1. INTEREST: LENDER SHALL CHARGE AN INTEREST RATE OF FIVE PERCENT (5%) PER ANNUM ON THE OUTSTANDING BALANCE OF THE PRINCIPAL AMOUNT FROM THE EFFECTIVE DATE UNTIL THE DATE OF REPAYMENT.

5.2. FEES: BORROWERS SHALL PAY TO LENDER A COMMITMENT FEE OF THREE PERCENT (3%) OF THE PRINCIPAL AMOUNT ON THE DATE HEREOF, AND A FEE OF ONE PERCENT (1%) OF THE PRINCIPAL AMOUNT ON THE DATE OF THE FIRST REPAYMENT INSTALLMENT.

6. 3. DEFAULT AND REMEDIES
6.1. DEFAULT: IF ANY BORROWER FAILS TO MAKE ANY PAYMENT WHEN DUE HEREUNDER, OR BREACHES ANY OTHER MATERIAL COVENANT OR OBLIGATION UNDER THIS AGREEMENT, SUCH FAILURE OR BREACH SHALL CONSTITUTE A DEFAULT HEREUNDER.

6.2. REMEDIES: UPON THE OCCURRENCE OF A DEFAULT, LENDER SHALL HAVE THE RIGHT TO DECLARE THE ENTIRE PRINCIPAL AMOUNT IMMEDIATELY DUE AND PAYABLE, TO WITHHOLD FURTHER CREDIT, AND TO TAKE ANY OTHER ACTION THAT LENDER DEEMS APPROPRIATE.

7. 4. REPRESENTATIONS AND WARRANTIES
7.1. BORROWERS REPRESENT AND WARRANT THAT THEY HAVE THE FULL POWER AND AUTHORITY TO ENTER INTO THIS AGREEMENT AND TO PERFORM THEIR OBLIGATIONS HEREUNDER, AND THAT THE EXECUTION AND DELIVERY OF THIS AGREEMENT AND THE PERFORMANCE OF THEIR OBLIGATIONS HEREUNDER DO NOT VIOLATE ANY LAW, REGULATION, OR ORDER, NOR DO THEY VIOLATE ANY CONTRACTUAL OBLIGATION TO WHICH THEY ARE A PARTY.

8. 5. COVENANTS
8.1. FINANCIAL REPORTING: BORROWERS SHALL PROVIDE LENDER WITH ANNUAL FINANCIAL STATEMENTS WITHIN NINETY DAYS AFTER THE END OF EACH FISCAL YEAR, AND QUARTERLY FINANCIAL STATEMENTS WITHIN FORTY-FIVE DAYS AFTER THE END OF EACH QUARTER.

9. 6. GOVERNING LAW
9.1. THIS AGREEMENT SHALL BE GOVERNED BY AND CONSTRUED IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE LAWS OF THE STATE OF NEW YORK WITHOUT GIVING EFFECT TO ITS CONFLICT OF LAWS PRINCIPLES.

10. 7. ENTIRE AGREEMENT
10.1. THIS AGREEMENT CONTAINS THE ENTIRE AGREEMENT BETWEEN THE PARTIES AND SUPERSEDES ALL PRIOR AGREEMENTS AND UNDERSTANDINGS, WHETHER WRITTEN OR ORAL, RELATING TO THE SUBJECT MATTER HEREOF.

11. 8. AMENDMENTS
11.1. NO AMENDMENT OR MODIFICATION OF THIS AGREEMENT SHALL BE VALID OR BINDING UNLESS IT IS IN WRITING AND SIGNED BY BOTH PARTIES.

12. 9. NOTICES
12.1. ALL NOTICES REQUIRED OR PERMITTED HEREUNDER SHALL BE IN WRITING AND SHALL BE DELIVERED PERSONALLY, BY REGISTERED OR CERTIFIED MAIL, RETURN RECEIPT REQUESTED, OR BY EMAIL TO THE ADDRESSES SET FORTH BELOW:

12.1.1. TO BORROWERS: NORTHBRIDGE CAPITAL PARTNERS LIMITED, 123 WALL STREET, NEW YORK, NY 10005, ATTENTION: GENERAL COUNSEL.
12.1.2. TO LENDER: [LENDER'S NAME], 456 BROADWAY, NEW YORK, NY 10006, ATTENTION: LOAN PORTFOLIO MANAGER.

13. 10. SEVERABILITY
13.1. IF ANY PROVISION OF THIS AGREEMENT IS HELD INVALID OR UNENFORCEABLE, THE REMAINDER OF THIS AGREEMENT SHALL REMAIN IN FULL FORCE AND EFFECT.

14. 11. ASSIGNMENTS
14.1. NEITHER PARTY MAY ASSIGN ITS RIGHTS OR OBLIGATIONS HEREUNDER WITHOUT THE PRIOR WRITTEN CONSENT OF THE OTHER PARTY.

15. 12. WAIVERS
12.1. NO WAIVER BY EITHER PARTY OF ANY BREACH OF ANY PROVISION OF THIS AGREEMENT SHALL CONSTITUTE A WAIVER OF ANY SUBSEQUENT BREACH OF THE SAME OR ANY OTHER PROVISION OF THIS AGREEMENT.

16. 13. MISCELLANEOUS
13.1. THIS AGREEMENT MAY BE EXECUTED IN SEVERAL COPIES, EACH OF WHICH SHALL BE DEEMED AN ORIGINAL, BUT ALL OF WHICH TOGETHER SHALL CONSTITUTE ONE AND THE SAME INSTRUMENT.

17. SIGNATURES
17.1. IN WITNESS WHEREOF, THE PARTIES HERETO HAVE EXECUTED THIS AGREEMENT AS OF THE DATE FIRST ABOVE WRITTEN.

